{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>If from a thread to a shoe strap.</b> By this Abraham showed the strength of his generosity: he did not wish to enjoy any of the spoil of the kings, even things that have no monetary value. And he swore concerning this, saying, ״I have lifted up my hand,״ which is an expression of an oath, in the manner of (Numbers 14:30): ״נשאתי את ידי.״ And he said, ״I have lifted up my hand to YHWH,״ — for everything is consecrated before Him — ״and if I take from anything that is yours.״ And for this reason he said הרימותי (I have lifted up) and did not say נשאתי (I have borne/lifted), because consecration is called תרומת יד, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 34): ״תרומת כסף ונחשת״:" "<b>And the Gaon</b> Rabbi Saadiah wrote: ״If from a thread to a shoe strap״ — Scripture mentioned the vegetative, the living, and the inert, which are all the categories of possessions that are under the dominion of one who speaks. ״From a thread״ — this is the vegetative, and it includes produce and fruits; ״and to a shoe strap״ — this is the living, and it includes beasts and fowl; ״and if I take״ — this is the inert, and it includes silver and gold and precious stones and pearls. And therefore he added and said: ״and if I take from anything that is yours,״ etc." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> ״If from a thread to a shoe strap.״ The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: You said, ״from a thread״ — by your life, I will give your children the commandment of tzitzit, which is called a thread, as is said (Numbers 15): ״ונתנו על ציצית הכנף פתיל תכלת,״ and they translate חוטא דתכלתא; and I will purify your children by means of the altar, which was surrounded by a crimson thread. You said, ״and to a shoe strap״ — by your life, I will give your children the commandment of the strap of tefillin, and the commandment of eating the paschal offering, in which it is written (Exodus 12): ״ונעליכם,״ and the commandment of yibum, in which it is written (Deuteronomy 25:9): ״וחלצה נעלו,״ and likewise with the expression of shoe I am destined to exact retribution from Esau, as is said (Psalms 60:10): ״על אדום אשליך נעלי,״ and likewise with the expression of shoe I will praise your children, as is said (Song of Songs 7:2): ״מה יפו פעמיך בנעלים בת נדיב.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:31.471510622Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}